0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":4,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I'm approving PKT-0078. The goal is met through the packet's own alternative, a cheaper style-cache key, and nothing else needs fixing.\n\n**What changed:** one file in the sdkjs fork, `word/Editor/Styles/style-cache.js` (commit `71f92b0`, +41/−12). `Shape.js` was not touched, and the diff is well within budget.\n\n**Correctness:**\n- **The key is exact.** It is the serialized `WriteToBinary` bytes held as a string, so two different styles can never share a key. That keeps the contract that resolved text styles stay identical. Long inputs are chunked at 8 KiB, so the `apply` call can't hit the argument-count limit.\n- **Switching to a `Map` changes no meaning.** An entry is added on first use, its count goes up on repeats, and it is deleted when the count reaches 0, the same as the old plain object.\n- **The remembered keys are safe.**\n  - When `remove` gets the cached object itself, it uses the key stored at `add` time and skips re-serializing.\n  - For any other object, it falls back to `getKey`, as before.\n  - When an entry's count reaches 0, its remembered key is dropped as well.\n  - One small difference: if a cached object were changed after caching, `remove` now still finds its entry. Before, that lookup would have missed. This is more robust, not a regression.\n- **The acceptance command passed**, as the factory reported.\n\n**Process:**\n- The Executor log is complete and corrects the packet's wrong premise. The style cache is called from `ParaRun.Get_CompiledPr`, not from `CShape.recalculateTextStyles`, and the log shows this with a call-chain profile.\n- The follow-up PKT-0085 is listed under Spawned packets and is already in the queue.\n- Every point from the earlier rejections is resolved. The code can now be reviewed on the fork branch, and the log states that the goal was met through the \"cheaper key\" alternative.\n- The measurements are recorded honestly: style-cache work fell from about 130 ms to about 24 ms per open. The end-to-end gain is inside the noise on this 2-CPU machine, and the log says so.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE exact string-key StyleCache removes sha256 cost (~130→24 ms), styles unchanged, fork branch reviewable, follow-up PKT-0085 spawned","ttft_ms":2653,"type":"result","duration_ms":18020,"uuid":"81eb2b2b-76c5-4b08-9623-860c2331c7ba","ttft_stream_ms":1037,"time_to_request_ms":452,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":101,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":34,"input_hooks":5,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":51,"tool_pool_refresh":5,"init_message":19,"init_frame_send":10,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":44,"message_prep":4,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":11,"request_announcements":44,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":10,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":55,"message_normalization":6,"client_creation":3,"request_build":35},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":249,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":186,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":204,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":129,"process_rss_mib_result":219,"process_anon_mib_result":130,"process_peak_rss_mib":223,"process_cpu_ms_turn":797,"process_wall_ms_turn":18019,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":311,"process_wall_ms_streaming":15269,"main_stream_count":4,"main_stream_event_count":253,"main_stream_chunk_count":75,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":8,"cpu_ms":19,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":23,"ambient_wait_ms":7,"render_ms":1,"producers":41,"token_counts":0},"first_content_frame_ms":1037,"time_to_request_from_spawn_ms":4717096,"warm_spare_claimed":false,"flag_fetch_kick":"started_in_init_warm","time_origin_ms":1793663411839.1707,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"process_start_tuning":0}
